Reviewed cumulative diff from base adf58cad3dc419d6a383355cf0479e846b5175dd and successor delta from 120e5202148e7a8703625f00474cc310f2d7ac40. Only tools/premerge-check.sh and tools/premerge-check-test.sh are in scope.

Independent exact-SHA archive: /private/tmp/storymodel-premerge-review.JeNHiv.
- committed shell court passed;
- bash syntax checks passed;
- base-to-candidate diff check passed;
- author receipt SHA-256 matched 0fae5586e616744475451b9d6a05013335d88ecb1c9800a9cdb66d0262955569.

The successor directly courts both omissions from my prior blocks: empty candidate_id fails closed, and a valid landed row beside a malformed identity row rejects the whole snapshot. I independently mutated the invalid-row branch from raise to continue; the committed court exited 1 at the mixed-row case because the mutated checker falsely reconciled the valid row. The precise partial-parser mutation is killed.

Unique landed and landed_out_of_band rows remain the only exemptions. Pending, abandoned, superseded, unknown, missing phase, missing or empty identity, duplicate OID, command failure, malformed JSON, and contradictory landability remain fail-closed. No candidate source edits, landing authorization, or scope expansion.
